  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Partnering for Resilience to Emergencies through Transformation of SRHR (PRET-SRHR)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">- To strengthen the capacity of the weakest health systems to deliver rights-based SRH services that are resilient in the face of conflict and disaster in fragile settings;
- To transform harmful social and gender norms that inhibit access to SRHR in fragile settings
- To strengthen regional accountability for ensuring SRHR for women and girls in humanitarian and fragile settings</narrative>
  </description>
